<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kenya</h1><p class="st-meta">1963 CE – present · capital Nairobi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">East Africa's leading economy, independent since 1963, which moved from one-party rule to a multi-party democracy with a new constitution in 2010.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kenya-colony">Kenya Colony</a> became independent on 12 December 1963 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta">Jomo Kenyatta</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenya-african-national-union">Kenya African National Union</a> (KANU), after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mau-mau-rebellion">Mau Mau</a> emergency and negotiations at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancaster-house">Lancaster House</a>. It became a republic a year later, with Kenyatta as president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta">Kenyatta</a> built a centralised state, favouring capitalist development, land purchase by Africans and close ties with the West, while tourism, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> drove growth. Daniel arap Moi, president from 1978, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenya-african-national-union">KANU</a> the sole legal party in 1982. Domestic and foreign pressure restored multi-party politics in 1991, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwai-kibaki">Mwai Kibaki's</a> victory in 2002 ended KANU's rule.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>A disputed election in 2007 led to violence that killed more than 1,000 people, followed by a power-sharing deal and a new constitution in 2010 that devolved power to 47 counties. Kenya remains a republic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ruto">William Ruto</a> president since 2022.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kenya.jpg" alt="Kenya" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:Pumbaa80 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kenya.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Yea